This is not an open-source licence. It is a source-available licence: the source is
public so you can read it, learn from it and change it for your own use, but the
right to use it commercially is reserved.

You may read, study and modify this software. You may use and redistribute it free
of charge under the conditions below.

1. GRANT FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE

   You may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute and sublicense this
   software free of charge, provided the use is Non-Commercial as defined in
   section 2 and the copyright notice above is kept in all copies.

   Non-Commercial use includes, without limitation:

     a) personal use by an individual, regardless of skill, hours worked or
        whether the resulting mod is published;
     b) use on mods, modpacks, resource packs, servers or other projects that
        generate no revenue of any kind, including donations that are not a fee
        for the output;
     c) use by a non-profit, a school or a charity, where the work is not sold.

2. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A LICENCE

   Commercial Use means any use from which money is earned, directly or
   indirectly. It includes, without limitation:

     a) selling, or bundling for sale, a mod, modpack, texture pack, server,
        service or other product produced with this software;
     b) performing paid work for a client using this software, including
        freelance and contract work;
     c) use by or for an incorporated entity, studio, publisher, or any team
        acting in the course of a business, whether or not the output is sold;
     d) use where the software is a material part of a paid offering, including
        hosting, support or as part of a subscription.

   You may not engage in Commercial Use without a valid commercial licence
   granted in writing by the copyright holder.

3. COMMERCIAL LICENCE AND PRICE

   A commercial licence is available for a base fee of AUD $50 (fifty Australian
   dollars), payable once, per licensee, for a term under section 3.1.

   ONE LICENCE COVERS EITHER:

     (a) ONE SOLO DEVELOPER — a single individual doing paid work, on any number
         of projects, with no revenue share owed on those projects; or

     (b) ONE SERVER — a single Minecraft server, network or hosting operation,
         however many people work on it internally, provided the software is not
         resold or sublicensed to third parties.

   A business with two or more paid developers, or someone operating two or more
   servers, needs one licence per person or per server respectively.

   Obtain one by opening an issue at
   https://github.com/mechwarriorpro/mccodeingtoolver1/issues
   or contacting ShadowClanGaming through GitHub.

   3.1  PERIOD. The base fee covers a term of TWELVE MONTHS from the date the
        licence is issued. Continued Commercial Use after the term expires needs a
        renewal at the then-current rate.

   3.2  WHAT THE BASE FEE COVERS. Use by one licensee, on any number of machines,
        for any number of projects, with any revenue level. There is no revenue
        share, no per-seat charge and no royalty on projects covered by a valid
        licence.

   3.3  COMBINATIONS AND VOLUME PRICING. Licences bought together are priced as
        follows, applied to the total number of licences in the purchase:

          | Licences | Discount | Price per licence |
          |----------|----------|-------------------|
          | 1–24     | none     | AUD $50.00        |
          | 25–49    | 10%      | AUD $45.00        |
          | 50–74    | 25%      | AUD $37.50        |
          | 75–99    | 40%      | AUD $30.00        |
          | 100+     | 50%      | AUD $25.00        |

        The price is per licence, so the total at a quantity break is less than
        the total just below it — seventy-five licences at $30 cost less than
        seventy-four at $37.50. Where that happens, ordering the higher quantity
        is permitted and cheaper.

        The maximum discount is 50%. The price never falls below AUD $25 per
        licence, whatever quantity is bought.

   3.4  RESALE. A licensee may not resell, sublicense or redistribute this software
        to third parties as a commercial offering of their own; that needs a
        separate written agreement.

   3.5  GST. The price is in Australian dollars. If GST applies to the licensee, it
        is charged in addition.

   3.6  PRICE CHANGES. The published rate applies to licences issued after a change
        is announced. A licence already issued runs to the end of its term at the
        rate that was paid.

4. NO RE-LICENSING

   You may not sublicense this software under different terms, and you may not
   remove or alter this notice in a way that hides the restriction in section 2.
   Distributing a modified copy is permitted only under this same licence.

5. UNLICENSED COMMERCIAL USE — RETROACTIVE FEE

   Commercial Use without a valid commercial licence (section 2) is not
   permitted, and this section sets the fee payable for it. It does not grant
   permission: the use is a breach of this licence while it continues, and
   paying the fee does not make past use lawful except as stated here.

   5.1  RETROACTIVE LICENCE FEE. For any period of Commercial Use without a
        licence, the user is liable for a retroactive licence fee payable to the
        copyright holder, calculated as the greater of:

          (a) FIFTEEN PER CENT (15%) of all revenue earned from the project or
              activity during that period, as a royalty; or

          (b) the base commercial fee under section 3 (AUD $50 per licence, at the
              single-licence rate and NOT the discounted combination rate),
              pro-rated for the period of unlicensed use and charged at DOUBLE that
              rate, with a minimum of ONE base fee. Where the unlicensed use covers
              several developers or servers, one licence per person or server is
              counted.

        The greater of the two applies, so the 15% royalty is never the only
        figure: a project with undisclosed or uncertain revenue is still liable
        for a sum that can be calculated from the price list. Worked at the base
        rate, a year of unlicensed use by one developer or server is AUD $100
        (double the annual fee); a quarter is a quarter of that, with the minimum
        applying. Unlicensed use is charged at the single-licence rate, so the
        combination discount can never be used to make a breach cheaper.

   5.2  WHAT COUNTS AS REVENUE. Revenue includes sales, subscriptions, service
        fees, server income, donations received as a fee for the output, and
        advertising or sponsorship income, in each case for the project or
        activity for which this software was used, before platform and payment
        processing fees.

   5.3  PAYMENT. The fee is payable within 30 days of written demand by the
        copyright holder. The copyright holder may also recover reasonable costs
        of recovery, including legal costs.

   5.4  RECORDS. A user liable under this section must, on written demand,
        provide a written statement of the revenue on which the fee is
        calculated, within 30 days. Failing to provide it does not stop the
        liability; where revenue cannot be established, limb (b) of section 5.1
        applies.

   5.5  THIS IS NOT A LICENCE. Nothing in this section permits continued
        Commercial Use. A user who wishes to continue must obtain a commercial
        licence under section 3. Section 5.1 charges for the period already used.

6. TERMINATION

   Any use in breach of this licence terminates your rights under it
   automatically. On termination you must stop using and distributing the
   software. The copyright holder may pursue any remedy available for use without
   a licence, including for the period before the breach was discovered. Payment
   of a fee under section 5 does not by itself restore the right to use the
   software.

